.TH TERM-NOTIFY-SOUND 1 "2026-06-30" "cmdblocks" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
term-notify-sound \- emit a terminal-aware completion notification
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B term-notify-sound
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B term-notify-sound
plays a lightweight terminal notification. It writes a WezTerm OSC user
variable when running in WezTerm, touches a state-file signal for VS Code-style
terminals, and falls back to a terminal bell for unknown terminals.
.PP
When running inside tmux, OSC sequences are wrapped for tmux passthrough. If
.I /dev/tty
is unavailable, the helper attempts to write to the current pane TTY.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/term-notify/signal
Signal file touched for VS Code-style terminal integrations.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The notification was emitted or intentionally ignored after best-effort
fallbacks.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux-copy-last-output (1)
